      ],
      "explanation": "A negative exponent means taking the reciprocal, so\n\\[\n2^3=8,\\qquad 2^{-3}=\\frac1{2^3}=\\frac18.\n\\]\nThe denominator is \\(\\frac18+\\frac18=\\frac14\\), which is nonzero. Therefore\n\\[\n\\frac{2^3+2^3}{2^{-3}+2^{-3}}\n=\\frac{8+8}{\\frac18+\\frac18}\n=16\\div\\frac14\n=\\boxed{64},\n\\]\nchoice E.",
